{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-maintained Excel locale data. CLDR does not carry either of these:",
    "spreadsheet format-code letters and error values are Microsoft's, not Unicode's.",
    "",
    "dateTokenAliases: Excel accepts number-format date codes written in the UI",
    "language, so a German workbook may carry 'jjjj-mm-tt' where the canonical",
    "code is 'yyyy-mm-dd'. Pairs are applied longest-first over a quote-aware",
    "scan. Only languages whose letters map unambiguously are listed; Hungarian",
    "and Turkish are omitted because their letters collide across fields (Turkish",
    "'s' is both saat/hour and saniye/second), which cannot be resolved by",
    "substitution alone.",
    "",
    "errors: Excel's localized error values, in ExcelError declaration order:",
    "Null, Div0, Value, Ref, Name, Num, Na. Languages absent here fall back to",
    "the English values.",
    "",
    "errorSuffix: Codcel's own annotation appended to an error message, not",
    "something Excel emits. Listed only for languages where the phrasing is",
    "unambiguous; anything absent falls back to the English text."
  ],
